    "q-352256": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352256",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $y=x-3{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis. Calculate the volume $V$ of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis. Do not round the answer.\n\n$V=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x(1-3x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$ So, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$  \n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1/3}x(x-3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1/3}({x}^{2}-3{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{4})|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =2\\pi [(\\frac{1}{3\\cdot {3}^{3}}-\\frac{3}{4\\cdot {3}^{4}})-0] \\\\  & =2\\pi (\\frac{1}{324}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{162}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
